# Changelog

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- support for limit parameter in tsio/insertion_dates

### Changed
- replaced sqlalchemy with sqlhelp
- switch off binary protocol for multi-statement schema initialization
- normalize lisp expressions before storing in cache

### Fixed
- api/set_cache_policy no longer crashes when setting already set series
- tables updated for tshistory_formula bound groups changes

## [0.9.2] - 2025-03-05

### Added
- comprehensive documentation overhaul:
  - installation and upgrade guides
  - basic, medium, and advanced tutorials
  - security documentation (basic auth and oidc setup)
  - excel addin documentation
  - scraping framework documentation
  - data mesh section
  - performance and caching guides
  - tasks management documentation
- models namespace for kvstore
- cachepolicy for editor proposals
- interval migration preparation
- operation.vacuum column

### Changed
- moved stores schema initiation to refinery_pro
- switched to new configuration object
- use tempconfig in tests
- moved hash64 to tshistory.util
- integrated tsview schema
- switched postgresql port to 5434 for server usage
- updated copyright years
- improved upgrade path documentation from 0.8.3

### Fixed
- schema init in init-db command
- drop table order in migration
- pytype compatibility (removed dead code)
- merged duplicate migrations for same versions
- documentation requirements

### Removed
- obsolete cli commands

## [0.9.1] - 2024-10-25

### Added
- setuptools version specification in pyproject.toml

### Changed
- cache series_lock_ready implementation now uses postgresql advisory locks for robustness
- ci moved to heptapod
- bumped dependencies

### Fixed
- cache refresh lock vulnerability to hard crashes (now transactional)

### Removed
- ready attribute from schema (replaced by transactional locking)

## [0.9.0] - 2024-08-01

### Added
- tswatch fully integrated into refinery
- kvstores integration with three namespaces: tswatch, dashboards, balances
- dbcache integration
- favicon for webapp
- infer_freq utility to compute frequency of timestamps
- required roles on http routes for security
- tshistory 0.20 migration available as task
- propagate parameter to tsio/rename
- __sig__ methods for search ui support

### Changed
- switched from refinery.cfg to tshistory.cfg (configuration consolidation)
- webapp module renamed from webapi
- cache system simplified (removed policy readiness status)
- history implementation now driven from tshistory.tsio
- editor reimplemented in elm (moved to tsview)
- formula-batch page moved to tsview
- wsgi now uses nosecurity middleware for permissions
- today operator renamed to now (following tshistory_formula)
- upgraded to python 3.11 and bookworm

### Fixed
- cache refresh_now better from_value_date computation
- force liveness when cache idates declared stale
- reduce_frequency no longer stops on empty stamps sequence
- keepnans keyword now required for updates with nans
- various deprecation warnings

### Removed
- refinery.cfg.template (replaced by tshistory.cfg)
- editor_callback (folded into tsview)
- separate historic view (integrated into tsview)
- proxyfix from wsgi
- permissions callback passing

## [0.8.3] - 2023-09-25

### Added
- rework schema requirement in init-db command

### Changed
- updated dependencies
- schema cleanup

### Fixed
- rework requirement in conftest for tests

## [0.8.2] - 2023-09-11

### Fixed
- http client missing index value causing platform-dependent behavior

## [0.8.1] - 2023-09-07

### Changed
- bumped dependency versions
- forced minimum required package versions
- documentation improvements with better chapter ordering

### Fixed
- readthedocs build section structure compatibility
- api documentation errors
- formula documentation fixes

## [0.8.0] - 2023-08-11

### Added
- scraping framework infrastructure for writing scrapers declaratively
- __version__ attribute in package root
- pyproject.toml with pytype and ruff configurations
- tox configuration
- automatic migration system
- search filters for cached series and series with specific cache policies
- minimal docstrings to api methods
- significant documentation updates for operators

### Changed
- removed rename view from cockpit
- removed metadata column from formulas view (scalability)
- adapted to tshistory source handling changes
- adapted to tshistory_formula typing changes
- specialized test machinery for refinery-specific routes
- reorganized schema initialization using base object inheritance
- downloadformulas now provides csv that can be re-ingested without transformation

### Fixed
- api.rst tshistory section in documentation
- readthedocs python version requirement (3.9)
- remote source schema initialization in tests
- explicit source specification to avoid config file interference

### Removed
- xl section from documentation (not for normal usage)
- deprecated apimaker helper function

## [0.7.0] - 2023-02-24

### Added
- sphinx documentation with pydata theme
- readthedocs configuration
- tests for cache refresh of autotrophic series
- tests for series with resample and slice operators
- find method to api documentation

### Changed
- cache now produces more revisions for formulas with today operator
- adapted to tshistory internal_metadata consolidation
- adapted to tshistory_formula schema simplification
- documentation reorganization and improvements

### Fixed
- insertion_dates handling for autotrophic operator
- list-series-lock cli command
- cache behavior with formulas containing today operator (infinite revisions)

## [0.6.0] - 2022-12-26

### Added
- license file
- missing pypi classifiers
- refinery.cfg configuration template
- suspended_policies context manager to temporarily suspend active cache policies

### Changed
- refresh_series renamed from refresh for clarity
- cache refresh now uses underlying caches when refreshing (performance improvement)
- better presentation of series batches during refresh
- improved cache scope handling in refresh operations

### Fixed
- unnecessary formula calls for out-of-bounds value dates but in-bounds insertion dates
- priority_origin now requires explicit request
- cache no longer interferes with formula hijacking
- insertion dates now properly use intermediate caches

### Removed
- tshistory_editor (absorbed by tsview)

## [0.5.0] - 2022-10-11

### Added
- support for past uncached revisions in get, insertion_dates, and history
- ability to read leftwards out-of-cache data
- cache ui moved to tsview for common library sharing
- ability to specify port in webstart cli command
- not null constraint on cache schema

### Changed
- first cache entry now maximally populated for consistent series horizon
- improved cache refresh error handling (logs failing series instead of stopping)
- simplified live path extraction to separate method
- better nocache parameter propagation through all api layers
- use url_for for static resources in templates

### Fixed
- policy_by_name query returning wrong policy
- set_policy_series validator usage
- cache invalidation warning when deleting non-existent series cache
- values_markers_origins cache compatibility
- cache expansion on query-less requests
- cache lock handling with finally statement

## [0.4.1] - 2022-07-25

### Added
- basic readme documentation for setup

### Changed
- cache ui: policies list now displayed as html table for better column alignment
- pinned minimal package versions for dependency resolution

### Fixed
- missing tshistory_xl dependency
- missing schema.sql file in package
- web interface no longer fails on missing nginx/segment config entry

### Removed
- unused import log from web interface

## [0.4.0] - 2022-06-28

### Added
- comprehensive cache system for formula series:
  - cache policies with horizon definitions and scheduling rules
  - look_before/look_after attributes for smart horizon management
  - cache refresh functionality with initial import vs regular refresh
  - cache invalidation on formula changes
  - support for nocache and live parameters
  - automatic cache management for renamed/deleted formulas
- cache ui (elm-based):
  - policy management (create, edit, delete)
  - series association/dis-association with policies
  - schedule/unschedule policies
  - force refresh functionality
  - validation and error reporting
  - filters for cached and free series lists
- cache api endpoints:
  - create/edit/delete policies
  - associate/dis-associate series
  - query cache status
  - force refresh
- cli commands:
  - install cache schema
  - setup tasks
  - refresh cache manually
- cockpit moved from tshistory to refinery

### Changed
- config file name aligned with tshistory.cfg
- blueprint architecture for better template/static handling
- cache refresh order optimized (dependency order)
- smarter cache expansion to avoid unnecessary remote queries
- separated initial cache import from regular refresh

### Fixed
- cache handling across namespaces
- cache propagation for nocache and live parameters
- federation boundary cache invalidation
- concurrent cache refresh protection
- timezone handling for revision dates

### Removed
- from_date policy parameter (simplified initial import)
- prune parameter support (retired from tshistory_formula)

## [0.3.0] - 2022-01-13

### Added
- complete api integration

### Changed
- excel parts moved to tshistory_xl (refinery now only does final assembly)
- tshistory_rest and tshistory_client now integrated into tshistory core

### Fixed
- missing dependency
- removed involuntary dependency on proprietary package

## [0.2.0] - 2021-09-21

### Added
- tshistory_formula extended http handler integration

### Changed
- webapi now uses tshistory_formula http handler (previously in tshistory_rest)
- updateformulas now handles utf-8 format for csv files (windows compatibility)

### Fixed
- compatibility with tshistory_rest changes

## [0.1.0] - 2020-12-11

### Added
- initial release combining tshistory with components for full integration server side
- formula upload with metadata handling
- web api integration
- basic test suite
